 "stimulus_html": "<p>“An attack was made on Thursday last by a party of Insurgents under Shays, upon the troops commanded by General Shephard at Springfield. . . . Shays retreated that night to Ludlow, and the next day marched to Chicabee.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Hampshire Gazette Newspaper in Massachusetts Account of Shays’ Rebellion, January 1787</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615030,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The “Insurgents” described in the newspaper article provided were most likely influenced by which of the following?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1168092,
     "content_html": "Heavy taxes levied by the British government to pay for French and Indian War debt"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168093,
     "content_html": "Increasing taxes levied by the states to pay American Revolutionary War debt"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168091,
     "content_html": "Attacks by American Indians on the frontier that threatened their settlement"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168090,
     "content_html": "The risk of oppressive plantation owners striking out against individual enslaved people"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615031,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What was an indirect result of the turmoil caused by actions such as the one described in the article provided?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1168096,
     "content_html": "The First Continental Congress"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168095,
     "content_html": "The Boston Massacre"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168094,
     "content_html": "The Boston Tea Party"
    },
    {
     "id": 1168097,
     "content_html": "The Philadelphia Convention"
    }
   ],
